# Recipes API

A simple RESTful API built with Go and MongoDB for managing recipes.  
Includes full CRUD functionality and uses Docker-based MongoDB in tests with Testcontainers.

---

##  Features

- Create, read, update, and delete recipes
- Built with Gorilla Mux and the official MongoDB Go driver
- Modular structure for config, handlers, and models
- Test suite using `testcontainers-go` to spin up MongoDB containers
- Environment configuration with `.env` files
- Ready to deploy or extend

---

## Tech Stack

- Go 1.20+
- MongoDB
- Gorilla Mux
- Testcontainers-Go
- Docker (for testing)

---

##  Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/recipes-api.git
cd recipes-api
go mod tidy
```


## Configuration

Create a .env file in the root of the project:
```
DB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017
DB_NAME=recipesdb
```
### Running Tests

Tests will spin up a temporary MongoDB container using Testcontainers.
```
go test ./...
```
To avoid cached test results:
```
go clean -testcache
```
## Running the Server

Start your MongoDB instance locally, then:
```
go run .
```
The server will be available at http://localhost:8080.
📬 API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/recipe	Create a new recipe
GET	/recipe/{id}	Get a recipe by ID
PUT	/recipe/{id}	Update a recipe
DELETE	/recipe/{id}	Delete a recipe
GET	/recipes	Get all recipes